# Who has to look at a change before it lands.
#
# This file does nothing on its own. It takes effect when the ruleset on `main`
# gains a pull-request rule with "require review from Code Owners" — without
# that, a CODEOWNERS entry is documentation. It is written now because the
# entries below are the ones worth having the moment that rule is added, and
# because naming the files that decide who can read what is useful even while it
# is only advisory.
#
# The list is deliberately short. A CODEOWNERS that covers everything reviews
# nothing: it makes every PR wait on the same person and teaches everyone to
# route around it. What is here is the set of files where a mistake is not a bug
# but a breach.

# Default: everything else.
*                           @sarath200795

# ── The enforcement boundary ────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# These two files ARE the access control for a multi-tenant system holding
# occupational health records. There is no middleware behind them and no server
# to fall back on: the browser talks to Firestore directly, so a rule that is
# one `match` too wide is the whole of the exposure. Every change here should be
# read by someone other than its author, and should arrive with tests.
/firestore.rules            @sarath200795
/storage.rules              @sarath200795
/tests/                     @sarath200795

# ── The pipeline that deploys them ──────────────────────────────────────────
#
# A change here can ship rules, functions and hosting, and holds the service
# account that can do it.
/.github/workflows/         @sarath200795
/.github/dependabot.yml     @sarath200795

# ── Cryptography and the server tier ────────────────────────────────────────
#
# policy.js decides which fields are encrypted and under which key class; a
# field quietly removed from it is stored in the clear from that commit on, and
# nothing else in the system would notice. claims.js mints the token claim
# storage.rules enforces on. retention.js decides what gets destroyed.
/src/shared/crypto/         @sarath200795
/functions/lib/claims.js    @sarath200795
/functions/lib/retention.js @sarath200795
/functions/lib/fileDelete.js @sarath200795

# ── The record of what is known ─────────────────────────────────────────────
